{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used","id":1326263,"title":"What is the best, most ridiculous improvised weapon you've ever used?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-20T08:05:53-07:00","id":1326263,"title":"What is the best, most ridiculous improvised weapon you've ever used?","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/improvised-weapons\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/HH394.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/improvised-weapons\" target=\"_blank\"> Improvised Weapons &ndash; The Handbook of Heroes </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/improvised-weapons\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/improvised-weapons </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:IBMPlexSans\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">How did you stunt with it?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:29:39-07:00","id":1326269,"title":"","content":"Back in 1e, when DBT allowed for ridiculous Strength ratings (getting you up to about where the descriptions on the chart stopped on Strength alone), I contemplated using large sections of scenery and structures for this purpose, but never got to do anything like it in play. One example would be tearing up a long section of fencing to use as a Brawl-based fighting chain or seven section staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:50:40-07:00","id":1326277,"title":"","content":"In 2e, my circle journeyed into The Labyrinth in search of their captured circle-mates. Along the way, I (the GM) had them slowly gain temporary derangements in the form of Limit Breaks with the control effect. The Sidereal in the group ended up with the controlled Deliberate Cruelty. When they get to the lair of the big bad, they come across a torture chamber. This was just for flavor and not an important rule, but the Sidereal's player asked me if there were any torture pliers, and I said sure. He took and pocketed them.<br /> <br /> At the end of the lair, they face the Big Boss, who ends up using that Necromancy spell that turns you into a &quot;final form&quot; (I think it's acronym was BOSS?) and it was a big epic fight. Well the Sidereal did this stunt where he pulls out the pliers and uses them as an improvised weapon to pull out on of the monsters enormous teeth and then stab it in the eye with it's own tooth. I was so impressed with the stunt using a tool the player picked up hours earlier as a role-playing moment and used it to be DELIBERATELY CRUEL in fighting this monster; I gave him a 3 point stunt, and this ended up being the deathblow for the boss. <br /> <br /> A truly epic moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:58:27-07:00","id":1326280,"title":"","content":"Oh you know, the usual. Yeddim. Chunks of Juggernaut's rotting flesh. Poisoned earing. Soup cup. Paper clip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:40:08-07:00","id":1326289,"title":"","content":"Other PCs is generally the classic.<br /> <br /> One of my friend used Cascade of Cutting Terror with a guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:46:23-07:00","id":1326293,"title":"","content":"Princess Magnificent with Lips of Coral and Robes of Black Feathers, in a late 1e, early 2e DB game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T10:34:18-07:00","id":1326299,"title":"","content":"Lunar swordfish...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T16:04:08-07:00","id":1326360,"title":"","content":"In emulation of the Chuck Norris joke of old, one of my Abyssals once plucked out one of his beard hairs and tried to skewer three men through the heart with it; sadly, due to bad dice rolls, he only managed it on two. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T16:56:04-07:00","id":1326367,"title":"","content":"In 2.5 our ST gave us each a custom charm based on something we did or fit our character. My Socializer had the ability to pull a paper fan out of his sleeve with a single word written on it (Disappointment, Flirt, etc...). Our Dawn got the ability to manifest a chandelier to swing on, errol flynn style, which he once dropped on the juggernaught that Mask of Winters uses to hold up his castle. our Zenith took a macguffin indestructible pillar and ripped it from the ground, put it on his shoulder and carried it back to the ship. When the DBs attacked us in the street, he two hand pillar smashed one of them- but not like a club or a bat. he used the pillar vertically and brought it straight down on the head of the DB like smooshing an ant with your finger. Also there's the one time i tricked a bunch of wyld hunt pirates into the hold of an air ship and then used it as a ram to end a siege by maxing out the engines and shoving a fan in the gears. it turns out priceless irreplacable artifacts of the first age make excellent explosives for the purpose of breaking a regular old stone wall","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:26:06-07:00","id":1326381,"title":"","content":"One time, one of my mortal players used a pot of simmering soup as a weapon when the party got ambushed on the trail. He used the hot liquid to blind and burn the enemies, then used the iron cookpot to break bones and crush skulls.<br /> <br /> Of course, that <i>was</i> the dinner for the party, so once he did that they no longer had anything else to eat for that day other than trailbread, so the other characters were not nearly as chuffed as he was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:59:13-07:00","id":1326384,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, I need to use hardtack as an improvised weapon one of these days.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne game session I made the stuff for the players, to make their sailing experience more &quot;authentic.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b(I also served dry peas, salt pork, and grog.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-20-2019, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T20:20:36-07:00","id":1326393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326384#post1326384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, I need to use hardtack as an improvised weapon one of these days.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne game session I made the stuff for the players, to make their sailing experience more &quot;authentic.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b(I also served dry peas, salt pork, and grog.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dwarven bread can be used as a hammer, a club, a crowbar, armor, and furniture. In truly desperate times, you can even eat it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T10:06:06-07:00","id":1326483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326393#post1326393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dwarven bread can be used as a hammer, a club, a crowbar, armor, and furniture. In truly desperate times, you can even eat it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Discworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T10:12:54-07:00","id":1326484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326483#post1326483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ask me, actual hardtack is unpleasant enough; I don't think you need to go baking gravel into it or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T10:17:42-07:00","id":1326485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326484#post1326484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ask me, actual hardtack is unpleasant enough; I don't think you need to go baking gravel into it or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, won't deny that fact.<br /> <br /> But my doubt was related to Sorcerous Overlord's &quot;dwarven bread&quot; comment being a possible Discworld citation, if memory tricks me not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T15:31:01-07:00","id":1326540,"title":"","content":"We were doing a modern-day Exalted game in which my character, a teenage Dawn Caste, was sparring with a slightly older Solar.<br /> <br /> She jumped up onto a fire escape, so naturally he took hold of the fire escape, tore it off the building and smashed it into the pavement with her still on it.<br /> <br /> It worked a lot better than I expected.<br /> <br /> (The ST did not actually check my Strength+Athletics on that one, so I'm not at all sure whether my character should really have been able to do that to the poor fire escape or not, but whatever. No sense interrupting an entertaining stunt with additional math.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T16:04:41-07:00","id":1326547,"title":"","content":"At sea, got attacked by giant kraken. <br /> <br /> Main mast + Rigging + Phantom Arrow Technique = dead monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T19:50:17-07:00","id":1326584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326485#post1326485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, won't deny that fact.<br /> <br /> But my doubt was related to Sorcerous Overlord's &quot;dwarven bread&quot; comment being a possible Discworld citation, if memory tricks me not.</div> </div> </div> </div>bingo. The Scone of Stones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T19:55:32-07:00","id":1326588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326584#post1326584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bingo. The Scone of Stones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, i knew that was familiar. thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T20:02:47-07:00","id":1326589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1326263-what-is-the-best-most-ridiculous-improvised-weapon-you-ve-ever-used?p=1326393#post1326393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dwarven bread can be used as a hammer, a club, a crowbar, armor, and furniture. In truly desperate times, you can even eat it</div> </div> </div> </div>Dwarf bread is great. If you have dwarf bread, you'll never go hungry. For, if you have dwarf bread, absolutely <b>anything</b> will seem edible so that you don't need to eat the dwarf bread: raw sheep, your own shoes, rocks, piping hot magma, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T21:27:35-07:00","id":1326603,"title":"","content":"Before this becomes the Terry Pratchett thread, I\u2019d like to list another improvised weapon\u2026<br /> <br /> Today\u2019s game session revealed that the Evening Master Brueghel of the Council of Entities once murdered an Abyssal with\u2026 a sixty-foot silkworm caterpillar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T11:40:51-07:00","id":1326762,"title":"","content":"On topic: paired mules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12111-the_larz","name":"the_larz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T11:46:54-07:00","id":1326764,"title":"","content":"Zenith used a temple column the other day XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T21:34:34-07:00","id":1326874,"title":"","content":"Way back in a gonzo 1E game I was in our characters fought a Lunar Akuma that would spit balefire webs at people. My character wasn't overly the brightest, but also had zero scruples and one hell of a greedy streak. ST called for a roll to figure out what of value could be scavenged, which I proceeded to botch. There was the obvious stuff that couldn't really be hand-waved like any moonsilver and such, but the ST decided I was absolutely certain that web it had spit on an ally was priceless. My character stuffed it in an iron cauldron and started carrying it around. Eventually he realized that, while it was worthless in coin, he could fish it out of the cauldron with a big metal stick and fling it at people.<br /> <br /> The second isn't a weapon, per se, but in another game I played a Righteous Devil stylist who stunted using Cloud of Ebon Devils as a big area attack. (Which started with easily one of my silliest questions in a game, &quot;Hey, what happens if I INTENTIONALLY botch?&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:03:40-07:00","id":1326882,"title":"","content":"Back in 2e I had a player uproot a tree, and then rather than clubbing his enemies with it he jumped on it and proceeded to do skateboard stunts with it as a way to swing it around and simply used the mass of the tree spinning through the air from the stunts as his form of attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T15:25:41-07:00","id":1327083,"title":"","content":"That gives me the visual of someone with an oversized war hammer that's too unwieldy to swing traditionally using it like a seesaw to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T16:32:47-07:00","id":1327087,"title":"","content":"Our ath supernal used a temple pillar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T20:43:29-07:00","id":1327843,"title":"","content":"I recently had a lunar PC use a potato as an improvised weapon. She was fighting down in a root cellar and grabbed a potato off the wall as a weapon. She ended the fight by shoving the potato down her opponent's throat, all the way into his chest cavity, and replacing his heart with it. She ripped the heart back out and immediately drank it for his form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25150-siegward-of-catarina","name":"Siegward of Catarina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25150_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}